.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt IOREMAP 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ioremap ,
.Nm iounmap
.Nd create and destroy uncached kernel MMIO mappings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/resource.h
.Ft void *
.Fn ioremap "resource_size_t phys_addr" "size_t size"
.Ft void
.Fn iounmap "void *addr"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn ioremap
function reserves the requested physical MMIO range, maps it into a dedicated
kernel VA arena, and returns an uncached kernel pointer.
The
.Fn iounmap
function tears down a mapping created by
.Fn ioremap .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn ioremap
function returns the mapped kernel pointer on success or
.Dv NULL
on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr request_mem_region 9 ,
.Xr resource 9
